  "summary": "Knight Office is a Microsoft 365 adversary-in-the-middle phishing kit whose Python Flask operator console is used to monitor captured sessions and replay stolen tokens, sidestepping passwords and MFA. Victims are drawn in via a self-spoofed DocuSign-style lure, a Monday.com open redirect and a compromised Joomla site, then handed a device authentication code for Microsoft's deviceauth flow. Stolen tokens are replayed from data-center and proxy infrastructure using the python-requests/2.34.2 user agent, followed by rogue Entra device registration and a Windows Hello for Business key credential.",
